1. React kya hai?Library hai UI banane ke liye. Facebook ne banayi.
Feature: Component based, Virtual DOM se fast hai,

2. JSX - HTML jaisa dikhne wala JSHTML nahi hai, JS hi hai jo HTML jaisa dikhta hai.
HTML se farak: class nahi className, for nahi htmlFor, har tag close karna padega, andar JS likhne ke liye {} lagta hai.

3. Real DOM: Asli wala, heavy hai, direct change karoge to poora page slow.
Virtual DOM: React ka halka-phulka copy. Pehle is copy me change karta hai, fir Real DOM se compare karke sirf utna hi badalta hai.

4. Reconciliation / DiffingReact kaise compare karta hai yehi Reconciliation hai.
Rule simple hai - key dekhega, type dekhega, agar same hai to sirf andar ka data badlega, poora component nahi todega. Isiliye fast hai.

5. Components - Functional vs ClassClass wala: Purana, this.state, render() likhna padta tha. Ab koi use nahi karta.
Functional wala: Naya, simple function. Hook use kar sakte ho.

6. PropsParent se child ko data bhejne ka tareeka. Immutable hai - matlab child usko change nahi kar sakta, 
sirf padh sakta hai. Data flow hamesha upar se neeche - One-way.

7. State & Lifting State UpState: Component ki apni memory.
Lifting: Agar 2 bhaiyo ko same data chahiye to data ko unke Papa me rakh do. Papa se dono ko props me bhej do.

8. Controlled vs Uncontrolled
Controlled: Input ka data React ke useState me hai. Har letter type hote hi state update. Hum control me hain.
Uncontrolled: Input ka data DOM me hai, hum useRef se baad me nikalte hain.
Yaad karne ka tarika: Controlled = Remote hamare haath me, Uncontrolled = TV par jaake button dabana

9. Keys - Aadhaar CardPehle hi bataya tha, list me har item ka unique ID. Index kabhi mat do, bug aayega.

10. Fragments - Extra div se bachaoReact ko ek parent chahiye, par faltu div se UI kharab hota hai. Isliye <> </> use karo.

11. Conditional Rendering
If-else JSX me direct nahi chalta.

javascript{isLogin ? <Logout /> : <Login />}
{isAdmin && <AdminPanel />} // Agar isAdmin true hai to hi dikhega

12.  Refs - useRef, createRef, forwardRefuseRef: Functional me use hota hai, re-render nahi karwata.
createRef: Class component wala, har baar naya ref banata hai - functional me use mat karo.
forwardRef: Child ka input Parent se control karna ho to. React 19 me forwardRef ki zarurat nahi, direct prop me ref bhej sakte ho.

13.  Portals - Component ka BhootKisi component ko uske parent ke bahar render karna. 
Jaise Modal, Popup. DOM me woh body ke andar lagega par code me kahin bhi likho

14. Error Boundaries - MistriKoi ek component crash hua to poori app crash nahi honi chahiye.
Error Boundary usko pakad leta hai. Ye abhi bhi Class se hi banta hai.

15. Strict Mode - Police WalaKoi galat kaam kar rahe ho to development me 2 baar render karke warning deta hai. Production me kuch nahi karta.

16. HOC - Higher Order ComponentEk aisa function jo component lega aur naya powerful component dega.

